/-!
# GeoSeq stage V10-3: the fields of `tab:primepower` (and of the improved and new rows)

Generated by `scripts/gen_v10_3_fields.py`. Each `GF<q><tag>` is the power-basis model `PF p d fc` of
`𝔽_q = 𝔽_p[x]/(f)`, `f = x^{d+1} + ∑ fc_i x^i`; its `Field` instance takes the inverse from a table of codes and the
kernel checks `a · a⁻¹ = 1` for every `a ≠ 0` (`decide +kernel`), which certifies that `f` is irreducible.
The digit code is `PF.code` (power basis, `sec:primepower`).
-/

namespace GeoSeq

-- `priority := high`: other modules declare instances `Fact (Nat.Prime p)` too (e.g. `fact_prime_11`, V4Defs); a fixed
